{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01O0:statement", "parent_tag": "01NS", "chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "definition", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent sheaf of\ngraded <MATH_0003>-algebras. The\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>relative homogeneous spectrum of <MATH_0004> over <MATH_0005><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>,\nor the <TEXTITOPEN_0002>homogeneous spectrum of <MATH_0006> over <MATH_0007><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>, or the\n<TEXTITOPEN_0003>relative Proj of <MATH_0008> over <MATH_0009><TEXTITCLOSE_0003> is the scheme\nconstructed in Lemma <REF_0001> which represents the\nfunctor <MATH_0010> (<REF_0002>), see\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nWe denote it <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_S$", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it ", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{A}$", "MATH_0009": "$S$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-glue-relative-proj}", "MATH_0010": "$F$", "REF_0002": "\\ref{equation-proj}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-glueing-gives-functor-proj}", "MATH_0011": "$\\pi : \\underline{\\text{Proj}}_S(\\mathcal{A}) \\to S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-relative-proj}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:2426c096bedc59aa0f6bece1e80cb3b42bdef6e2b970d0718908caa8d0e068db", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c6351f29bde6b8c3595121f640463bff4ac339a9f396dfa312b9d2bcbcbe2309", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ddf9030cf88f0b5526e012ab83eddfe7111ec8348868d077d66092d81b88a4bf"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01NS:prose-0004", "parent_tag": "01NS", "chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe relative Proj comes equipped with a quasi-coherent\nsheaf of <MATH_0001>-graded algebras\n<MATH_0002>\n(the twists of the structure sheaf) and\na ``universal'' homomorphism of graded algebras\n<MATH_0003>\nsee Lemma <REF_0001>. We may also think of this\nas a homomorphism\n<MATH_0004>\nif we like. The following lemma is a formulation of the\nuniversality of this object.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathbf{Z}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\bigoplus_{n \\in \\mathbf{Z}}\n\\mathcal{O}_{\\underline{\\text{Proj}}_S(\\mathcal{A})}(n)$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\psi_{univ} :\n\\mathcal{A}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\pi_*\\left(\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{n \\geq 0}\n\\mathcal{O}_{\\underline{\\text{Proj}}_S(\\mathcal{A})}(n)\n\\right)\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-glue-relative-proj-twists}", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\psi_{univ} :\n\\pi^*\\mathcal{A}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{n \\geq 0}\n\\mathcal{O}_{\\underline{\\text{Proj}}_S(\\mathcal{A})}(n)\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:be38c8318555077138acf22cd17e8f8edf440a229576e40291dba4a6bfa3d04c", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b5f301de5ae6ad7c0a37fee8c182f39d364fa3b7f0335658cda8aa157d96ec0e", "source_math_hash": "sha256:271a61dbf4e4596255815bf7d8e6de7deb796b651fdcd2a8141c2ce182f8ba05"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01O1:statement", "parent_tag": "01NS", "chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "In Situation <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0001>\nbe a quadruple. Let\n<MATH_0002>\nbe the associated <MATH_0003>-morphism.\nThere exists an isomorphism\nof <MATH_0004>-graded <MATH_0005>-algebras\n<MATH_0006>\nsuch that the following diagram commutes\n<MATH_0007>\nThe commutativity of this diagram uniquely determines <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{situation-relative-proj}", "MATH_0001": "$(f : T \\to S, d, \\mathcal{L}, \\psi)$", "MATH_0002": "$r_{d, \\mathcal{L}, \\psi} : T \\to \\underline{\\text{Proj}}_S(\\mathcal{A})$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathbf{Z}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_T$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\theta :\nr_{d, \\mathcal{L}, \\psi}^*\\left(\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{n \\in \\mathbf{Z}}\n\\mathcal{O}_{\\underline{\\text{Proj}}_S(\\mathcal{A})}(nd)\n\\right)\n\\longrightarrow\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{n \\in \\mathbf{Z}} \\mathcal{L}^{\\otimes n}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{A}^{(d)} \\ar[rr]_-{\\psi}\n \\ar[rd]_-{\\psi_{univ}} & &\nf_*\\left(\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{n \\in \\mathbf{Z}}\n\\mathcal{L}^{\\otimes n}\n\\right) \\\\\n &\n\\pi_*\\left(\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{n \\geq 0}\n\\mathcal{O}_{\\underline{\\text{Proj}}_S(\\mathcal{A})}(nd)\n\\right) \\ar[ru]_\\theta\n}\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$\\theta$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-tie-up-psi}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:e460849fe61f4050a3f7457213fb511e19106dd3f2167f3c721f2a70a845c3f3", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c0582cf03c64c11a95829daa26852779a09efcda7150bd6374bbc8844f038db7", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9f16612d3342f22429c29ee0bc95d528d17e495b6372e3e8854820d8534de240"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01O1:proof", "parent_tag": "01NS", "chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "proof", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Note that the quadruple <MATH_0001>\ndefines an element of <MATH_0002>. Let\n<MATH_0003>\nbe the locus\nwhere the sheaf <MATH_0004>\nis invertible and generated by the image of\n<MATH_0005>.\nRecall that <MATH_0006> represents the functor <MATH_0007>, see the proof\nof Lemma <REF_0001>. Hence the result will follow\nif we can show the quadruple\n<MATH_0008>\nis the universal family, i.e., the representing object in <MATH_0009>.\nWe may do this after restricting to an affine open of <MATH_0010> because\n(a) the formation of the functors <MATH_0011> commutes with base change\n(see Lemma <REF_0002>), and (b) the pair\n<MATH_0012>\nis constructed by glueing over affine opens in <MATH_0013>\n(see Lemma <REF_0003>).\nHence we may assume that <MATH_0014> is affine. In this case the functor\nof quadruples <MATH_0015> and the functor of triples <MATH_0016> agree\n(see proof of Lemma <REF_0004>) and moreover\nLemma <REF_0005>\nshows that <MATH_0017>\nis the universal triple over <MATH_0018>.\nGoing backwards through the identifications in the proof of\nLemma <REF_0006> shows that\n<MATH_0019>\nis the universal quadruple as desired.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(f : T \\to S, d, \\mathcal{L}, \\psi)$", "MATH_0002": "$F_d(T)$", "MATH_0003": "$U_d \\subset \\underline{\\text{Proj}}_S(\\mathcal{A})$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_{\\underline{\\text{Proj}}_S(\\mathcal{A})}(d)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\psi_{univ} : \\pi^*\\mathcal{A}_d \\to\n\\mathcal{O}_{\\underline{\\text{Proj}}_S(\\mathcal{A})}(d)$", "MATH_0006": "$U_d$", "MATH_0007": "$F_d$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-relative-proj}", "MATH_0008": "$(U_d \\to S, d, \\mathcal{O}_{U_d}(d), \\psi_{univ}|_{\\mathcal{A}^{(d)}})$", "MATH_0009": "$F_d(U_d)$", "MATH_0010": "$S$", "MATH_0011": "$F_d$", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-proj-base-change}", "MATH_0012": "$(\\bigoplus_{n \\in \\mathbf{Z}}\n\\mathcal{O}_{\\underline{\\text{Proj}}_S(\\mathcal{A})}(n),\n\\psi_{univ})$", "MATH_0013": "$S$", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-glue-relative-proj-twists}", "MATH_0014": "$S$", "MATH_0015": "$F_d$", "MATH_0016": "$F_d$", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-relative-proj-affine}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-proj-functor-strict}", "MATH_0017": "$(d, \\mathcal{O}_{U_d}(d), \\psi^d)$", "MATH_0018": "$U_d$", "REF_0006": "\\ref{lemma-relative-proj-affine}", "MATH_0019": "$(U_d \\to S, d, \\mathcal{O}_{U_d}(d), \\psi_{univ}|_{\\mathcal{A}^{(d)}})$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:70bc954bc97ede3ff75de7034fa77445ccf86042f6e300e549badfcab416a17c", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:12dbc882413ff790971d559fc34107c0256040539f5501ad704150caf0d0cd81", "source_math_hash": "sha256:39cc0433f39153a8fbb8a6a4111bca0d650e486479f89745b3f59faadf3a1dad"}
